    CurrentValue[
     EvaluationNotebook[], {TaggingRules, "ResourceCreateNotebook"}]],
   ImageSize->Automatic]],ExpressionUUID->
  "62f76333-f8ae-4b81-a0c9-44d0da3c850f"]
}], "Subsection",
 Editable->False,
 Deletable->False,
 TaggingRules->{"TemplateGroupName" -> "LongDescription"},
 DefaultNewCellStyle->"Text",
 CellTags->{"Basic Description", "LongDescription", "TemplateCellGroup"},
 CellID->97826971,ExpressionUUID->"15c9791e-e994-449c-89ee-e7f1112d4664"],

Cell["\<\
AntennaLink is a high-performance Wolfram Language paclet that brings \
professional-grade electromagnetic antenna simulation directly into your \
computational notebooks. It tightly integrates the industry-standard NEC-2 \
(Numerical Electromagnetics Code) engine via Wolfram LibraryLink. This \
enables blazing-fast parameter sweeps and provides immediate access to \
segment-level currents, far-field radiation grids, and impedance \
characteristics.\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules->{},
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990029358202345*^9, 3.990029365481456*^9}, {
  3.990029908245531*^9, 3.990029955479491*^9}},
 CellTags->"DefaultContent",
 CellID->312061637,ExpressionUUID->"1a36b046-69db-4d5c-a2ff-1ef1e005f095"],

Cell["\<\
Beyond the raw solver engine, the paclet provides a suite of high-level \
constructive geometry builders that allow you to easily generate complex \
structures like Yagi-Uda arrays, helical coils, and parabolic mesh reflectors \
with just a few parameters. Whether you are analyzing mutual coupling between \
parasitic elements, conducting broadband S-parameter sweeps, or modeling the \
effects of lossy Sommerfeld ground planes, AntennaLink abstracts away the \
tedious bookkeeping of wire segmentation and excitation tagging so you can \
focus on the RF design.\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules->{},
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.990029358202345*^9, 3.990029366680682*^9}},
 CellTags->"DefaultContent",
 CellID->544441387,ExpressionUUID->"ab5a465a-7beb-48e3-9d5c-7b103d36348c"],

Cell["\<\
Finally, AntennaLink truly shines through its 3D visualizations. With simple, \
out-of-the-box functions, you can plot physical antenna geometries \
dynamically colored by induced current magnitudes and phases, or render \
stunning 3D polygon surfaces of far-field radiation lobes seamlessly overlaid \
on your structural models. This rich visual feedback loop makes AntennaLink \
not just a robust numerical solver, but a powerful interactive sandbox for \
electromagnetic education and antenna design exploration.\
\>", "Text",
 TaggingRules->{},
 CellChangeTimes->{3.990029358202345*^9, 3.9900299802521467`*^9},
 CellTags->"DefaultContent",
 CellID->1470682059,ExpressionUUID->"d87a792f-2326-4f3c-afbc-136593984ac7"]
}, Open  ]],

